From d861a5ea426297380221d157c6a42342c0264161 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fi3 <you@example.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 01:24:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ADD selected-agent backend slash commands to avoid prompt
 resumes

Selected-agent slash input is routed through the backend command API, so commands such as /status and /fork produce provider-owned command output instead of being delivered as normal follow-up prompts. Codex handles these commands locally and records them in the session transcript without running codex exec resume.
